{"name":"Mamba Yellow","hex":"#fdd014","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mamba","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various venomous snakes of the genus Dendroaspis, native to Africa, that live in trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mamba"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mamba","blocks":[{"text":"Mambas are fast-moving, highly venomous snakes of the genus Dendroaspis in the family Elapidae. Four extant species are recognized currently; three are essentially arboreal and green in colour, whereas the black mamba, Dendroaspis polylepis, is largely terrestrial and generally brown or grey in colour. All are native to various regions in sub-Saharan Africa, and all are feared throughout their ranges, especially the black mamba. Africans have many legends and stories about mambas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Hartebeespoort_Zoo_and_snake_park%2C_Black_Mamba_-_panoramio.jpg/330px-Hartebeespoort_Zoo_and_snake_park%2C_Black_Mamba_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mamba","wikidata":"Q194425"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Dendroaspis.png/330px-Dendroaspis.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Dendroaspis.png/330px-Dendroaspis.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADendroaspis.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Mamba_Dendroaspis_angusticeps.jpg/500px-Mamba_Dendroaspis_angusticeps.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Mamba_Dendroaspis_angusticeps.jpg/1280px-Mamba_Dendroaspis_angusticeps.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Mamba_Dendroaspis_angusticeps.jpg/500px-Mamba_Dendroaspis_angusticeps.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMamba_Dendroaspis_angusticeps.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thu